From 41b4b3623cf42008680352656737a9f2453ffb58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:56:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Proposal (02-rights): WorkshopUse Grant in the Frontier
 program

A facility-use right, first kind only: the issuer lets one grantee run
one workshop holding with the grantee's own ore and wood, within a
number of uses, a number of arms and an expiry, without any key or
ownership moving. Two phases (ReserveUse escrows both sides in the
Grant, ConsumeUse settles them), ReleaseUse and RevokeGrant undo an
open reservation, CloseGrant returns the rent.

Kept out of every allocated table: tags 0xD0-0xD5 are routed before
the v2 tag table, codes 200-211 and the Grant layout live in
frontier_abi::v2::rights. No rules-kernel change, so the S1 ruleset
hash is unchanged. Not adopted; no PS2 record kinds yet (the verifier
would need them before any deployment).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C5Nj2bMRw3LSNvj17s1QPg
